I've been thinking about different ideas mostly because I'm an idea
junkie but also because my husband is thinking about implementing a
different version too - (though I doubt it will happen this century)
and that gave me a focus for my first suggestions. Here are some more:

I want a notebook that will let me make notes about the various levels -
of course notebooks are pieces of equipment like eveything else and if
you lose your ordinary boring marker you won't be able to write anything
new in it - you might also lose it or get it burned up...  You 'll
sometimes find other adventurers notebooks - which though mostly
irrelevant would be a way of sharing rumours (or spreading new ones!).
These notebooks might look like scrolls, spellbooks, or tools... 
as other TYPES of characters might speak different languages (hello
D&D) you might not be able to make out whats written in them if they
were of a different type - perhaps you'd have to polymorph yourself
to acquire such intrinsics.....

I want more dungeon graffiti - perhaps on dying the character that's
about to leave some bones behind could be granted a chance to write
their own message - limited to some unspecified random number of letters
so you get messages like:


I've got a +3 .......

where the characters dying words were not totally lost.

I want a spray can so I can write on walls.
I can also squirt monsters in the eyes with it.

How about some half-levels - lofts or cellars that are not the
next level above or below and into which the monsters also stroll.

Such half-levels would also allow some more complex puzzles... maybe
you would _have_ to levitate up into a loft to press the button that
lets you open the cellar door on one level  - the existence of the
loft's entrance above you would require some kind of message like:

"You feel a draft from above."

And of course bats would love such places.


How about an indicator to let you know how loaded up you are? I'd
like to know that my current load feels light -after all I'd know if I
was there!

I like small trashy stuff that isn't especially powerful but is fun. 
Like:

Crackers that have to be pulled with friendly monsters - perhaps a 
cracker carrying monster wearing paper hat and blowing one of those party
sqeakers that unroll would accost you and wouldn't let you past until
you'd pulled enough crackers and he'd won one! Inside there would be 
a cookie motto or a joke - anyone got a suitable set of hack jokes? - 
a paper hat and a plastic gift... it might be good for one use like
a lockpick that breaks after its opened its first chest, or a whistle
that works once but thereafter is silent. 


And I'd like to be able to invent new cookie rumours that go into the
local system's file - this would have to be limited in some way to avoid
someone being a real spoiler but it could be fun.  For instance my
character, Veronica the Valkyrie, reaches level 12 and is allowed to add
a new rumour. When it is read later it would look like:

Veronica-V says: "If you want to pick a fight, dig a hole, or smash
		   a chest, rob a delving dwarf."

so the reader is at least warned that the info was input locally!

Well, I've got to run, the pub for lunch is calling - how else can
vegetarian's escape the canteen's Halloe'en special of Witches Brew!

